            0.087
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.108,
            0.844,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Suppose you roll a 6-sided die 12 times and get a ‘3’ three times."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.135,
            0.8,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What is the experimental probability of rolling a ‘3’?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.16,
            0.773,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) What is the theoretical probability of rolling a ‘3’?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.184,
            0.885,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Why might these probabilities be different? What would you expect to happen if you roll the die 60, 600, or 6000 times?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.249,
            0.797,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.3 Elements of Probability: Sample Spaces and Events"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.317,
            0.357,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.3.1 Sample Space"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.346,
            0.885,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Recall that the sample space, denoted by S, is the list of all possible outcomes. Each possible outcome is called an element of the sample space."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.39,
            0.82,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The sample space S must include "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "every possible outcome",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.416,
            0.686,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• No outcome should be "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "listed more than once",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.443,
            0.884,
            0.482
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The number of elements in the sample space is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "sample size",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and is denoted by n(S)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.487,
            0.425,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Examples of Sample Space"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.516,
            0.883,
            0.557
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. The sample space for whether it rains tomorrow could be S = {Rain, No Rain} and the sample size n(S) = 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.56,
            0.883,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. The sample space for a match, i.e., the possible outcomes for a team playing — could be S = {Win, Lose, Draw} and sample size n(S) = 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.605,
            0.337,
            0.624
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Tossing a Coin:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.628,
            0.618,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Experiment: Tossing a fair coin once."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.649,
            0.64,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Sample Space: S = {Heads (H), Tails (T)}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.669,
            0.39,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Sample Size = 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.697,
            0.32,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Rolling a Die:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.721,
            0.686,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Experiment: Rolling a standard 6-sided die."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.742,
            0.571,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Sample Space: S = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.762,
            0.388,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Sample Size = 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.79,
            0.381,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Tossing Two Coins:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.813,
            0.615,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Experiment: Tossing two coins simultaneously."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.853,
            0.599,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sample Space: S = {HH, HT, TH, TT}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.874,
            0.39,
            0.892
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Sample Size = 4"
            }
          ]
        },
